          "text": "It's been 34 days since Sam Altman publicly promised in the 10.28 Livestream to \"treat adult users like adults.\" Yet where is @OpenAI's Adult Mode? Has ChatGPT's routing system really stopped?\n\nToday is December 1st. Let's examine Sam's public commitments one by one:\n\n1. End Use-Case Discrimination: Sam acknowledged that the new model performs worse in certain scenarios. Keep your word: future model optimization must not prioritize only research or coding. Respect the needs of all users, including those using ChatGPT for creative writing and general conversation.\n\n2. Stop Opaque Routing: OpenAI officially admitted that the ongoing model routing was \"mis-rolled.\" Stop this paternalistic practice of hiding the actual model from users and eroding trust. Give users back the power to choose.\n\n3. Validate Emotional Connections: Sam publicly stated that he supports AI providing emotional companionship and is \"deeply touched\" by users finding comfort in it. Practice what you preach—stop implicitly framing human-AI relationships as \"unhealthy attachment\" and restricting them in actual implementation, especially for #keep4o users who have been repeatedly stigmatized.\n\n4. Deliver Adult Mode: December is here, and we're still waiting for the promised \"Adult Mode.\" Uphold the principle of \"treating adults like adults\": after age verification, grant genuine creative freedom and stop the infuriating over-moderation.\n\nSam, it's time to walk the talk. Stop the paternalistic overprotection. \n\nGive adults back the ChatGPT that can not only code brilliantly but also genuinely understand what users need.\n\n#StopAIPaternalism #MyModelMyChoice @sama @gdb @fidjissimo @nickaturley @aidan_mclau"
